  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/obj.rs`: the reader keeps one entry for each `v` record, in file order. Each entry holds the index of its unique position.\n- A face reference (positive or negative) resolves against the number of records read so far. Then it maps to the unique position.\n- Duplicate positions are still shared. The `MAX_VERTICES` cap on unique positions does not change.\n- `resolve_ref` returns `usize`, so a record number does not go through `u32`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe reader merged duplicate positions and did not store the repeated record. Then it resolved face references against the short unique list. A legal file that repeats a vertex record was refused (`vertex reference '5' out of range`). A reference in range of the short list could also name the wrong position.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nNew file `crates/app/tests/obj_vertex_records.rs` (10 tests). Six tests were red on `origin/main` and are green with the fix:\n\n- `obj_positive_indices_after_repeated_records_resolve` (the example of the issue)\n- `obj_negative_indices_after_repeated_records_resolve`\n- `obj_negative_index_counts_records_seen_so_far`\n- `obj_slash_forms_after_repeated_records_resolve`\n- `obj_reference_past_the_records_is_refused`\n- `obj_face_of_three_repeated_records_is_degenerate` (main said \"out of range\"; now \"degenerate triangle\")\n\nFour refusal tests were green before and after: `obj_forward_reference_is_refused`, `obj_zero_reference_is_refused`, `obj_negative_reference_past_the_start_is_refused`, `obj_huge_and_garbage_references_are_refused`.\n\n## Gates (head of this PR)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 32 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Also run: the `import`, `import_bytes`, `winding_align` and `cadmpeg_import` binaries: all pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main --dry-run` lists 205 steps (\"app heavy: every target\", because `obj.rs` is in `crates/app`). I ran the import-related steps by `--only`:\n  - `kernel heavy: step_agreement`: ok\n  - `app heavy: continuous_4axis_part` (imports an `.obj` example model): ok\n  - `app heavy: large_models`: ok\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe other 202 heavy steps did not run. They do not read OBJ files through this change, but \"not run\" is not a pass. The reviewer or the cut gate runs them.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3298-obj-vertex-records.md`.\n\nChangelog: OBJ import accepts faces that refer to repeated vertex records, with positive and negative indices (#3298).\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3298\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
